## Propagating Trace Context Across RabbitMQ

The issue is that RabbitMQ doesn't automatically carry W3C `traceparent`/`tracestate` headers. You need to manually inject context into message headers on publish and extract it on consume.

**Service A (Publisher) – Inject context:**

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using OpenTelemetry;
using OpenTelemetry.Context.Propagation;
using RabbitMQ.Client;

// Create an ActivitySource for your producer
private static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceA.Producer");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void PublishOrder(Order order)
{
    using var activity = Source.StartActivity("order.publish", ActivityKind.Producer);

    var props = channel.CreateBasicProperties();
    props.Headers ??= new Dictionary<string, object>();

    // Inject current trace context into message headers
    Propagator.Inject(
        new PropagationContext(activity.Context, Baggage.Current),
        props.Headers,
        (headers, key, value) => headers[key] = value);

    channel.BasicPublish("orders-exchange", "order.created",
        basicProperties: props,
        body: JsonSerializer.SerializeToUtf8Bytes(order));
}
```

**Service B (Consumer) – Extract context:**

```csharp
private static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceB.Consumer");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void HandleMessage(BasicDeliverEventArgs ea)
{
    // Extract trace context from incoming headers
    var parentContext = Propagator.Extract(
        default,
        ea.BasicProperties.Headers,
        (headers, key) =>
        {
            if (headers != null && headers.TryGetValue(key, out var val))
                return new[] { Encoding.UTF8.GetString((byte[])val) };
            return Enumerable.Empty<string>();
        });

    Baggage.Current = parentContext.Baggage;

    // Start a new activity linked to the extracted parent
    using var activity = Source.StartActivity(
        "order.process",
        ActivityKind.Consumer,
        parentContext.ActivityContext);

    // Process the message — all downstream spans are now parented correctly
    var order = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Order>(ea.Body.Span);
    ProcessOrder(order);
}
```

**Key setup in both services (`Program.cs`):**

```csharp
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(t => t
        .AddSource("ServiceA.Producer")   // or "ServiceB.Consumer"
        .AddAspNetCoreInstrumentation()
        .AddOtlpExporter());
```

**Why this works:** The W3C `traceparent` header (containing trace ID + parent span ID) is serialized into the AMQP message headers by the publisher. The consumer extracts it and uses it as the parent context for its new activity, stitching the two services into one distributed trace.

If you're using MassTransit or NServiceBus, they do this automatically. For raw `RabbitMQ.Client`, the manual inject/extract above is required.
